OR PRACTICAL – PRACTICAL NO. 4
Title
Updating (Replacement) Model using POM-QM for Windows
 
Aim
To solve an Updating (Replacement) problem using POM-QM software and determine the optimal replacement policy with the help of an example.
 
Theory
Updating (Replacement) models in Operations Research are used to decide:
•	When an item/equipment should be replaced
•	To minimize total cost, which includes:
o	Purchase cost
o	Maintenance/operating cost
o	Salvage value (if any)
As equipment ages:
•	Maintenance cost increases
•	Efficiency decreases
Hence, replacement becomes economically justified.
 
Types of Replacement Problems
1.	Replacement of items that deteriorate with time (gradual wear & tear)
2.	Replacement of items that fail suddenly (random failure)
👉 In this practical, we consider replacement due to deterioration.
 
Example Problem
A machine has the following data:
Year	Maintenance Cost (₹)	Salvage Value (₹)
1	1,000	7,000
2	2,000	5,000
3	3,500	3,000
4	5,000	1,500
5	7,000	500
Initial cost of machine = ₹10,000
Find the optimal year for replacement.

Software Used
POM-QM for Windows
 
Steps in POM-QM Software
Step 1: Open Software
•	Open POM-QM for Windows
Step 2: Select Module
•	Click on Module
•	Select Replacement / Equipment Replacement
•	Choose Replacement due to Deterioration
Step 3: Enter Problem Data
•	Enter Initial cost = 10000
•	Enter number of years = 5
•	Enter maintenance cost year-wise
•	Enter salvage value year-wise
Step 4: Solve
•	Click on Solve or Compute
Step 5: View Output
•	Software calculates:
o	Average cost per year
o	Optimal replacement period
 
Result
From the POM-QM output:
👉 The machine should be replaced at the end of the 3rd year, as the average cost is minimum at that point.
 
Conclusion
Using the Updating (Replacement) model in POM-QM, the optimal replacement time is determined efficiently. This helps management take cost-effective decisions regarding equipment replacement.
 
