📘 OR Practical No. 7
Decision Theory – I : Decisions Under Uncertainty
 
🎯 AIM
To study Decision Making under Uncertainty using Decision Theory and solve the problem with the help of POM-QM software.
 
📖 INTRODUCTION / THEORY
Decision Theory deals with making optimal decisions when the future outcome is unknown.
👉 Decision Under Uncertainty means:
•	Probabilities of states of nature are not known
•	Decision is based on criteria/rules, not probability
 
🔑 KEY TERMS
Term	Meaning
Decision Alternatives	Available choices
States of Nature	Future conditions beyond control
Payoff	Profit / loss for each decision
Payoff Table	Matrix showing outcomes
 
📊 CRITERIA USED UNDER UNCERTAINTY
1.	Maximax (Optimistic)
2.	Maximin (Pessimistic)
3.	Minimax Regret
4.	Laplace (Equal Probability)
 
🧮 EXAMPLE
A company must decide the size of plant to install.
👉 Alternatives
•	A1: Small Plant
•	A2: Medium Plant
•	A3: Large Plant
👉 States of Nature
•	S1: Low Demand
•	S2: Medium Demand
•	S3: High Demand
📈 Payoff Table (₹ in lakhs)
Decision	Low	Medium	High
Small Plant	4	4	4
Medium Plant	2	6	8
Large Plant	-3	3	10
 
✍️ CALCULATIONS
1️⃣ Maximax Criterion
•	Small: max = 4
•	Medium: max = 8
•	Large: max = 10
✅ Decision: Large Plant
 
2️⃣ Maximin Criterion
•	Small: min = 4
•	Medium: min = 2
•	Large: min = -3
✅ Decision: Small Plant
 
3️⃣ Laplace Criterion
(Assuming equal probability)
•	Small = (4+4+4)/3 = 4
•	Medium = (2+6+8)/3 = 5.33
•	Large = (-3+3+10)/3 = 3.33
✅ Decision: Medium Plant
 
4️⃣ Minimax Regret
Regret Table
Decision	Low	Medium	High	Max Regret
Small	0	2	6	6
Medium	2	0	2	2
Large	7	3	0	7
✅ Decision: Medium Plant (minimum regret = 2)
 
